[h1]Less Map Markers [Performance fix][/h1]

[b]Up to date for game version 1.2.x[/b]

Less Map Markers is a simple performance mod that reduces the visual quality and detail of map markers.

Map markers can cost a surprising amount of FPS, especially when there are many of them on screen. This mod tones them down and hides a lot of less important foreign markers, while still keeping your own important markers visible.

[h2]What it does[/h2]

The mod currently affects:

[list]
[*]City markers
[*]Market markers
[*]Raw goods markers
[*]Import/export markers
[*]Blocked vision markers
[*]Building, army, navy, and conquistador construction markers
[*]Fort and toll markers
[*]Supply depot and fort restoration markers
[/list]

For these marker types, your own markers stay visible, while many foreign markers are hidden or simplified.

Construction markers have also been made lighter on performance. Building construction markers use keyed static concept icons so each building keeps its own icon, while army/navy/conquistador construction uses static category icons. The progress ring is preserved without the expensive vanilla per-construction icon lookup. Raw goods/RGO and import/export map markers also use keyed static goods icons instead of per-marker goods icon accessors.

[h2]Gameplay[/h2]

This mod only changes how map markers are displayed.

It does not change gameplay, balance, AI, economy, or mechanics.
